          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:019c2ff0eea9629cc0f78add7a39f6091a49947b1619ede7773dfc8a29e63a7f:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_0af9e0f8f76648f6973b62ae4578140f",
      "statement": "PebbleTemplateProcessor.templateExists() only asks the Pebble Loader whether the resource exists (engine.getLoader().resourceExists()) and never parses or compiles the template, making it cheap to call once per candidate during the hierarchical resolver walk; a template with a syntax error still reports as existing and only fails when actually rendered.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://core/src/main/java/org/facet/templates/pebble/PebbleTemplateProcessor.java#L87-L108",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:3d29ef2f163401e680119ff9b7352961ddae2388b51ddbfb2c7479fee9dada80:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_b60485964e204e33bbd86becbf01ed90",
      "statement": "PebbleTemplateProcessor.process() wraps every exception Pebble can throw (loader, parser, and runtime errors, including failures inside custom filters) in a TemplateProcessingException; this fixed a prior bug where a missing error.html/errors/{code}.html produced an empty HTTP 500 body because Pebble's unchecked LoaderException escaped the renderer unhandled.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://CHANGELOG.md#L60-L64",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:026d76c40f8ef15a53390d0846becba1d726c09eeed31ffcc278f591a8948519:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://core/src/main/java/org/facet/templates/pebble/PebbleTemplateProcessor.java#L136-L158",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:6f0e09d1bd4a6238558b6ec3b47f35f0210bd000f02cecefbc7ca4b618fd453a:"
        }
      ]
